    "answer": {
      "short": "Construction shown. The two triangles satisfy the given conditions but are not congruent.",
      "worked": "Draw $AX$ horizontally and construct a $30^{\\circ}$ ray at $A$. Mark $C$ on the ray with $AC=8\\text{ cm}$. An arc with centre $C$ and radius $6\\text{ cm}$ meets $AX$ at two distinct points, $B$ and $B'$. Join $CB$ and $CB'$. Both triangles have $AC=8\\text{ cm}$, a side of length $6\\text{ cm}$ and angle $A=30^{\\circ}$. Their third sides $AB$ and $AB'$ have different lengths, so the triangles are not congruent. The given angle is not included between the two given sides.",
